  "id": "COMPOUND:22282 - PROTEIN:5035",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that seco-plakortolide K may interact with COR-L279 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct link being through the enzyme Sucrose porin. This compound is targeted by seco-plakortolide K, and in turn, (S)(+)Carvone, a known substrate of Sucrose porin, targets COR-L279. This indicates a potential pathway where seco-plakortolide K influences the activity of (S)(+)Carvone, which then affects COR-L279. Another possible route involves Alpha globin, which is also a target of seco-plakortolide K, and which in turn targets COR-L279 through a different biochemical mechanism. The evidence suggests that seco-plakortolide K may act as a modulator of a metabolic pathway that ultimately leads to the activation or inhibition of COR-L279. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with seco-plakortolide K potentially influencing multiple targets that ultimately converge on COR-L279.",
